## Chapter 17: Shadows in the Atrium
The air inside the ruined glass atrium grew cold.
The Gideon Prep leader took a step forward, his enchanted silver rapier humming with a crackling blue arc of lightning. Behind him, the two mages raised their glowing staffs, their eyes full of arrogant disdain as they stared at Anvil Ridge's dented gear.
"Three seconds," the Gideon leader said smoothly, adjusting his silk cuffs. "Drop the Tier-C tag, turn around, and walk back to your perimeter. Otherwise, my squad takes it by force under Assessment Rule 4, and your little Salvager gets his legs broken."
Tobias’s hands shook against his wooden crossbow stock. Renna's knuckles turned white on her tower shield's grip, her jaw locked in fierce, stubborn defiance. She knew they were outmatched—Gideon’s enchanted gear and high-tier classes gave them an absurd stat advantage. But she refused to drop the tag her team had bled for.
"We aren't dropping anything, Gideon," Renna snarled, stepping forward to cover her squad.
"Unfortunate," the Gideon leader sighed, flicking his wrist. "Mages, suppress the shield. I'll take the archer."
*Click.*
A tiny, almost imperceptible sound echoed through the high, vaulted ceiling of the atrium.
It was the sound of a rusted iron bolt slipping out of Kaelen’s fingers.
Kaelen didn't yell. He didn't drop his timid posture. With a subtle flick of his wrist using his **45 Agility**, he flicked the small iron bolt straight up toward the central, high-voltage junction box mounted on the atrium's ceiling beam.
*THWACK!*
The iron bolt struck the main power circuit, shattering the glass casing and shorting out the emergency solar capacitors.
*BANG!*
A bright cascade of orange sparks erupted above them, and instantly, every single overhead floodlight in the massive atrium went completely black. The silver daylight filtering through the dust-covered glass roof was swallowed by thick, impenetrable shadows.
"What the—?!" one of the Gideon mages yelled, his blue spell-fire sputtering.
"The power box blew! Mages, illuminate the room!" the leader barked, swinging his rapier defensively.
To normal humans, the sudden darkness was blinding.
To Kaelen, his **[Low-Light Spatial Perception]** engaged in a microsecond, rendering the entire dark atrium in crisp, grayscale clarity. Every marble pillar, every shattered glass shard, and the exact positions of all four Gideon cadets were painted clearly in his mind.
Using his **[Hive-Mind Synapse]**, Kaelen calculated their blind spots and reaction times.
*Three seconds of total confusion,* Kaelen thought.
He didn't activate **[Kinetic Overdrive]**—he didn't need to waste the cooldown on four arrogant high schoolers.
Kaelen stepped around Renna’s tower shield in a silent, fluid glide. His boots, lined with his custom high-density insoles, made zero sound against the cracked marble floor.
He reached the first Gideon mage in less than half a second.
Before the mage could finish casting his illumination spell, Kaelen's hand shot out from the dark, grabbing the tip of the wooden staff. With a short, precise twist using his **46 Strength**, Kaelen snapped the enchanted wood in two like a dry twig and drove his palm lightly into the mage's sternum.
*THUMP!*
The compact impact knocked every drop of air straight out of the mage's lungs. The kid collapsed onto his knees, gasping for breath, completely incapacitated without a single mark left on his coat.
Kaelen didn't pause. He pivoted on his heel, slipping behind the second mage. He reached out, grabbed the back of the student's heavy tactical collar, and slammed the kid's face downward into the side of a concrete support pillar.
*CRACK!*
The second mage went instantly limp, crumpling onto the floor like a sack of wet laundry.
"What's happening back there?!" the Gideon leader shouted, his sword flickering wildly with lightning as he backed away into the shadows. "Julian! Mark!"
The Gideon scout panicked, pulling out a flare casing and trying to strike the ignition pin.
Kaelen appeared directly beside him out of the pitch-black air. He caught the scout's wrist in an iron grip, squeezing just enough for the kid's fingers to go completely numb, dropping the flare. Before the scout could scream, Kaelen delivered a short, sharp chop to the side of his neck.
*Thump.*
The scout dropped like a stone.
Three seconds had passed. Three out of four Gideon cadets were unconscious on the marble floor.
The Gideon leader was left standing completely alone near the central control node, his rapier shaking violently as he swung it in blind arcs through the dark. Sweat poured down his face, his arrogant posture completely shattered.
"Who's there?!" he screamed, his voice cracking with sheer terror. "Ironclad?! Is that an Ironclad strike team?!"
Kaelen glided silently back to his original position behind Renna’s right shoulder. He fell backward onto his rear in the dust, let out a loud, pathetic gasp, and kicked an iron pipe across the floor.
*CLATTER!*
"AAAH! THEY'RE IN THE DARK! SOMETHING IS IN THE DARK!" Kaelen shrieked, making his voice sound hysterical, terrified, and utterly helpless.
At that exact moment, Tobias fumbled with his belt and struck a emergency chemical glow-stick.
*SNAP!*
A bright, neon-green light flooded the ruined atrium.
Renna held her tower shield high, her eyes wide as she scanned the room.
The green light revealed a scene of absolute absurdity. Three of the four Gideon Prep elites—students wearing million-credit corporate gear—were lying unconscious across the floor. The Gideon leader was backing away against the control node terminal, his face pale as chalk, his rapier trembling as he stared at the shadows in total panic.
"What... what just happened?" Tobias whispered, his mouth hanging open as he held the glow-stick. "Where is their team?"
"I-I don't know!" the Gideon leader stammered, his aristocratic voice shaking uncontrollably. "Something... something moved in the dark! It broke Julian's staff and knocked them out in two seconds!"
Renna looked around the room, bewildered. She looked at the three fallen elites, then looked back at Kaelen, who was huddled on the floor behind her shield, clutching his head and trembling like a leaf.
Renna's eyes softened, assumption taking over her mind instantly.
"It was a rogue shadow-prowler," Renna concluded, her voice low and tense as she raised her shield toward the ceiling rafters. "The noise from the Behemoth must have drawn a subterranean beast into the atrium rafters. The flash of the light circuit scared it off."
"A... a shadow-prowler?" the Gideon leader gulped, looking up at the dark ceiling in sheer terror.
"You want to stay here and fight it, Gideon?" Renna asked coldly, stepping up to the control node terminal. "Or are you going to pick up your squad and get out of our sector?"
The Gideon leader didn't hesitate for a single second. He scrambled to his feet, grabbed two of his unconscious squadmates by their collars, and began dragging them frantically toward the glass exit.
"This sector is cursed!" he yelled over his shoulder, his aristocratic pride completely gone. "Anvil Ridge can keep the damn node!"
He practically threw his teammates over the threshold and fled into the fog, disappearing back toward the commercial sector.
Silence reclaimed the marble atrium.
Tobias let out a long, ragged breath, letting his crossbow drop against his thigh. "Man... Sector-C is wild today. First a Behemoth trips on a pipe, then a shadow monster knocks out Gideon Prep."
Mina ran over to the control node, her sharp eyes scanning the terminal. "Forget Gideon! Renna, log the tag now while the node is clear!"
Renna stepped up to the terminal and swiped the glowing red Tier-C tag across the scanner plate.
*BEEP!*
The holographic leaderboard above the atrium flashed violently as the System Node updated the live rankings across the entire exercise zone.
**[Tag Registered: Tier-C Granite-Scale Behemoth (20 Points)]**
**[Squad ID: Anvil Ridge Squad 4]**
**[Current Overall Assessment Rank: #12]**
"Twelfth place!" Tobias shouted, jumping into the air with a fist pump. "Anvil Ridge Squad 4 is in TWELFTH PLACE overall!"
Renna stared at the screen, a breathless, triumphant smile breaking across her face. She turned around, looked at her team, and walked over to Kaelen, who was slowly pulling himself up from the dirt, dusting off his knees.
Renna reached out, placing both hands on Kaelen's shoulders, her amber eyes shining with deep, genuine gratitude.
"We held the line, Kaelen," Renna said softly, her voice filled with emotion. "No one got hurt, we knocked Gideon out of our sector, and we're in the top twelve. You did great staying calm through all that chaos."
"I... I just stayed behind your shield, Renna," Kaelen muttered, lowering his head and putting on a timid, embarrassed smile. "You're the one who held the node."
"We did it together," Renna corrected firmly, turning back to Tobias and Mina. "Let's secure the perimeter of this atrium. We hold this control node until the four-hour timer runs out."
As Renna and the squad began setting up defensive positions near the entrance, Kaelen leaned his back against a concrete pillar, adjusting the hidden, high-density bracers under his sleeves.
He looked up at the quiet, dark rafters of the atrium, a faint, unreadable glint flickering deep within his dark eyes.
His mask was intact. His squad was safe. His rank was secured.
And far out in the central core of Sector-A, where Leon Thorne and Ironclad Academy were currently slaughtering high-tier monsters for the camera drones, Kaelen could feel the deep, pulsing energy of far larger prey waiting in the dark.
